--- explain
One more "smallest so far", this time on a number property. Start with the first show and replace it whenever a show has a **lower** rating:

```js
if (snack.price < best.price) {
  best = snack;
}
```

Two of the twelve shows share the lowest rating, 8.0: The Crown and How I Met Your Mother. With `<`, the first one stays the best, because the second isn't *lower*, only equal.
--- task
Make `lowestRated(list)` return the **name** of the show with the lowest rating. On a tie, the first one wins. For an empty list, return `""`.
--- hint
Same shape as P26: the empty-list `if`, `let best = list[0];`, a loop that replaces `best` when `show.rating < best.rating`, and `return best.name;`.
--- hint
```js
function lowestRated(list) {
  if (list.length === 0) {
    return "";
  }
  let best = list[0];
  for (const show of list) {
    if (show.rating < best.rating) {
      best = show;
    }
  }
  return best.name;
}
```
--- starter
// P27. The lowest rating
// lowestRated(list) gives back the NAME of the show with the lowest rating.
// On a tie the first one wins. An empty list gives "".

